>> title: Beef Stew
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, dinner, one-pot, braise, potatoes, oven
>> counters: Diner, Meat and Three, One Pot
>> pairs-with: dinner-rolls
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: forgiving — an extra half hour in the oven only softens the beef further; the potatoes go to mush long before the meat minds
>> washing-up: the Dutch oven, a bowl to toss the beef with the flour in

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (160°C).

Toss @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 2-in cubes), @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}(30 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

Brown @&(~1)floured beef{}, @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{}.

Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(chopped), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) with @&(~1)browned beef{}.

Deglaze @&(~1)pot{} with @dry red wine{1%cup}(240 mL).

>> step: braise 325°F 1 1/2 hr
Braise @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{4%cup}(950 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs} covered at 325°F for ~{90%min}.

>> step: braise 45 min more
Add @carrots{4%large}(cut in 1-in lengths), @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; quartered) to @&(~1)stew{} and braise ~{45%min}.
